losed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2025-03-07T21:14:49Z","updated_at":"2025-03-07T22:17:33Z","closed_at":"2025-03-07T22:17:25Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in Godot 4.4.stable\nNot reproducible in Godot 4.3.stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.stable - Windows 10.0.19045 - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 2070 SUPER (NVIDIA; 31.0.15.5186) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-6700K CPU @ 4.00GHz (8 Threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nAfter updating to 4.4 I noticed sound effects having exaggerated transients. It sounds like compressor effect were baked into sounds that added extra starting transient.\nEasier to notice on snappy sounds with a lot of high frequency content at the beginning.\n\nExample from reproduction project I used to test.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d9272568-11ae-475f-86eb-8b525ca44ff7\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- create project with test sound playback using short audio samples\n- test sound playback from older Godot version or audio player apps against 4.4\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[sound_playback_changes.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19133712/sound_playback_changes.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.githu